    "site_desc": "The Scotty Creek bog flux tower is located in an organic-rich collapse-scar bog about 50 km south of Fort Simpson in the Taiga Plains of the Mackenzie watershed. The tower was installed in 2014 and operates an open-path EC system year-round running on solar power only. The collapse-scar bog is treeless and free of permafrost.",
